hadiths[4]{hadithnumber,text}:
"23605","Sufyan narrated to us, he said: O people, let none of you kill another; when you stone the Jamrah, stone it with pebbles like the pebbles of khadhf; and its isnad was read to him: Yazid from Sulayman ibn Amr ibn al-Ahwas from his mother ya'ni from the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him."
"23606","Hushaym narrated to us, Layth informed us from Abdullah ibn Shaddad from Umm Jundub al-Azdiyyah that she heard the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, where he poured forth, say: O people, upon you is calmness and dignity, and upon you is the like of the pebbles of khadhf."
"23607","Ali ibn Ishaq narrated to us, Abdullah informed us, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman informed us from Mansur ibn Abd al-Rahman from his mother from Umm Uthman daughter of Sufyan, who is the mother of the elder sons of Shaybah, Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman said: and she had given pledge to the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, called Shaybah and he opened, and when he entered the House and returned and finished and came back, then the messenger of the Messenger of Allah, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, that: Answer; so he came to him and he said: I saw in the House a horn, so conceal it."
"23608","Mansur said: Abdullah ibn Musafi' narrated to me from my mother from Umm Uthman daughter of Sufyan that the Prophet, peace and blessings of Allah be upon him, said to him in the hadith: For there should not be in the House anything that distracts those who pray."
